{"name":"Antler","hex":"#957a76","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Antler","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A city and village in North Dakota."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Antler"}],"entries":[{"title":"Antler","blocks":[{"text":"Antlers are extensions of an animal's skull found in members of the Cervidae (deer) family. Antlers are a single structure composed of bone, cartilage, fibrous tissue, skin, nerves, and blood vessels. They are generally found only on males, with the exception of reindeer/caribou. Antlers are shed and regrown each year and function primarily as objects of sexual attraction and as weapons."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/50/Red_deer_stag_2009_denmark.jpg/330px-Red_deer_stag_2009_denmark.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Antler"},{"title":"Antler (venture capital firm)","blocks":[{"text":"Antler is an early-stage venture capital firm founded in 2017, headquartered in Singapore. The firm is present in over 30 cities and has made over 1,500 investments in early-stage companies."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Antler_(venture_capital_firm)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/89/Antlers_at_the_start_of_the_season%2C_cervus_elaphus%2C_deinze%2C_belgium.jpg/500px-Antlers_at_the_start_of_the_season%2C_cervus_elaphus%2C_deinze%2C_belgium.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/89/Antlers_at_the_start_of_the_season%2C_cervus_elaphus%2C_deinze%2C_belgium.jpg/500px-Antlers_at_the_start_of_the_season%2C_cervus_elaphus%2C_deinze%2C_belgium.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Red deer at the beginning of the growing season","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAntlers_at_the_start_of_t